# iolinki Commercial License

## Overview

This document outlines the commercial licensing options for **iolinki**, an IO-Link Device protocol stack.

## Scope for new quotes

The product-family scope below applies to new quotes using version
2026-10-01-product-family-v2. Rights already granted or separately agreed remain
governed by their accepted agreement; this scope does not reduce those rights.

## License Tiers

### 🔧 Single Developer License
**Price**: €1,399 (One-time, Royalty-Free)

**Includes**:
- Full source code access
- One agreed, named product family; unlimited manufactured units and customers within that family
- 1 year of updates and bug fixes
- Email support (48h response time)
- License holder: one named individual; one developer seat
- Two onboarding hours: build/setup assistance, MCU/PHY wiring and callback review, and a written bring-up checklist
- Larger ports quoted separately

**Ideal for**: Independent developers, startups, small product lines

---

### 🏢 Team License
**Price**: €4,699 (One-time, Royalty-Free)

**Includes**:
- The same source code, documentation and reference release as Single Developer
- One agreed, named product family; unlimited manufactured units and customers within that family
- 1 year of updates and bug fixes
- License holder: the named legal company; up to 5 authorized developers
- Seats may be reassigned when engineers change
- Contractors working on the licensee company's projects count within those 5 authorized developers; subsidiary rights require a separate quote
- Priority email support (24h response time)
- Quarterly technical reviews
- Up to 8 total scoped integration hours (replaces the Single onboarding allowance; not 2 + 8 hours)
- Agree the board, compiler, PHY and validation tasks before scheduling; larger ports quoted separately

**Ideal for**: Engineering teams, consultancies, mid-size manufacturers

---

### 🏭 Enterprise License
**Price**: Custom (Site-wide, Royalty-Free)

**Includes**:
- Team source, documentation and support benefits; broader product scope by agreement
- Multiple product families, subsidiary rights and broader SDK redistribution by custom quote
- Unlimited developer seats (single site)
- Dedicated support channel
- Custom feature development (negotiable)
- On-site training options
- Extended warranty and SLA

**Ideal for**: OEMs, large manufacturers, multi-product deployments

